## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical reasoning on per-tenant quotas, config hot-reload via Docker Config, and lightweight canary routing in a docker-dca cluster.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for runtime config delivery
- Lightweight sidecar pattern for per-tenant quotas
- Token-bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Canary routing and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simplified quota sidecar sketch (pseudo)
const quotas = loadYamlFromConfig('quotas.yaml');
let buckets = {};

function handle(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Tenant required');
  const q = quotas[tenant] || quotas.default;
  const now = Date.now();
  let b = buckets[tenant] || { tokens: q.limit, last: now };
  const elapsed = Math.max(0, now - b.last);
  b.tokens = Math.min(q.limit, b.tokens + (elapsed * (q.refillRate || 1)));
  b.last = now;
  if(b.tokens < 1){ return res.status(429).send('Quota exceeded'); }
  b.tokens -= 1;
  buckets[tenant] = b;
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test quota correctness across tenants?
- How would you handle config validation errors and rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of per-tenant configuration via Docker Config, feature gating, and edge proxy routing in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for per-tenant rules
- Feature flag gating in API
- Traefik TLS and docker-dca wiring
- Lightweight bootstrap and config reload

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample Express middleware for feature gate
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = {};
try { flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/feature-flags.json','utf8')); } catch(e) { flags = {}; }
function featureGate(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-Tenant');
  const enabled = flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].includes('new-feature');
  if(!enabled) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
app.get('/new-feature', featureGate, (req,res)=>{ res.send('New feature access granted'); });
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you hot-reload the flags without restarting the API?
- How would you test isolation across tenants when flags change?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge routing with policy-driven gating and cross-DC deployment, plus observability and security concerns in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- TLS termination at the edge with Nginx
- Central policy engine (OPA) integration
- Per-tenant feature flag evaluation
- Cross-DC routing semantics
- Observability with Prometheus and OTEL

## Code Example

```rego
package featureflag.allow
default allow = false
allow {
  input.tenant == "tenant-A"
  input.flag == "new_feature"
}
```

```nginx
# Nginx map-based routing example
http {
  map $http_x_feature_flag $upstream {
    default http://api_v1;
    "new_feature" http://api_v2;
  }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    location /api/ { proxy_pass $upstream; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement cache invalidation for policy decisions?
- How would you test the canary routing?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of docker-dca basics, per-tenant gating, and config management in real deployments across DCs.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for feature flags
- Hot reload of config without restart
- Tenant-scoped feature gating via header X-Tenant-ID
- TLS termination with Nginx and cross-DC routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal per-tenant feature gating middleware
const fs = require('fs');
let features = {};
function load(){
  try{ features = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/flags.json','utf8')); }catch(e){ features = {}; }
}
load();
setInterval(load, 30000);
module.exports = function(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  if (tenant && features[tenant] && features[tenant].includes('payments')) return next();
  res.status(403).send('Feature disabled');
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate config schema and handle partial reloads?
- How would you extend to multiple features and tenants with minimal latency impact?
